\f1\fs22 Dunhilton\'92s salamander face looked two-dimensional even in the most favourable light. He sat across from from Gerry, fingers steepled, expression sour as Gerry flicked through a presentation on the wall screen.\
\'93Initial TMinusVirus deployment\'97\'94\
\'93The what?\'94 Dunhilton checked.\
Gerry smiled a concessionary smile. \'93The 
\f2\i Lentil
\f1\i0  virus achieved seventy-two percent mortality among exposed Elvi subjects on Bent Street Plaza,\'94 Gerry reported. He flicked to a map. \'93This is the Ghetto showing our initial drop of aerosol canisters. The T\'97Lentil Virus achieved comparable mortality rates with the initial release.\'94\
\'93That\'92s excellent, Gerry!\'94 Dunhilton effused. \'93Are we still on track to eliminate the Elvi population within thirty-six days?\'94\
Gerry stepped over a series of slides, remaining on each long enough for Dunhilton to see the red dots appearing on the map, making it look like the ground itself had caught a pox.\
\'93Regrettably no, your Supreme Corporateness.\'94\
\'93No?\'94 Dunhilton hardened.\
Gerry flicked to a graph showing a red curve.\
\'93I know the shape of that graph, Gerry. I like to call it the Asymmetric Disappointment Function. It\'92s the kind of graph that leads to dismissal and stunt-level flying lessons\'97without parachutes\'97into a pillow.\'94\
Gerry tried not to look at the graph. Deaths had escalated beautifully, magnificently; the graph shot up with the trajectory of a launched rocket. Then it rolled lazily over, slumped and fell. But it didn\'92t crash, it just levelled out, apparently off screen and beyond the maximum width of any spreadsheet in the history of the great Airborne Meritocracy.\
\'93It seems the Elvi have developed herd immunity,\'94 Dunhilton observed soberly.\
Gerry slumped and swallowed hard. He would have to get ahead of this. Like in many universes, Ulyssians knew the expression, 
\f2\i rip the Band-Aid off
\f1\i0 , but in this one, it was often associated with bleeding out, both metaphorical and physical. Even so, Gerry had to pick at the Band-Aid. He flicked to a new graph showing two more Asymmetric Disappointment curves. A legend identified one as 
\f2\i Evolution Elvi
\f1\i0 , the other 
\f2\i Gospel Elvi
\f1\i0 . The Evolution curve rose and fell faster. The Gospel curve rose later but higher, and stayed higher, much higher.\
\'93We converted Elvi to gospel music, and now 
\f2\i they
\f1\i0  are the ones we are killing faster,\'94 Gerry summarised. \'93At the projected rates, in fact. So there\'92s good news in that.\'94\
Dunhilton tapped the table quietly and held Gerry\'92s gaze.\
\'93That\'92s information,\'94 Gerry continued.\
\'93What makes the Gospel Elvi more susceptible.\'94 Dunhilton made sure it did not sound like a question.\
\'93Or what makes the Evolution Elvi less susceptible.\'94 Gerry flicked to the next slide. It showed a man walking out of a shopfront that advertised itself in its display window as American Sound Studios. \'93This is Anthony Chantara. He was arrested on charges of not-for profit terrorism.\'94\
Dunhilton shrugged officiously. \'93If you say so.\'94\
\'93He was the guy the Elvi busted out of Truth Central.\'94\
Dunhilton recalled. \'93I sent a lot of people on extended holidays for that. We never recaptured hum?\'94\
\'93As far as we can tell, he\'92s been holing out in the Ghetto. Something of a celebrity. They call him the Great Teacher.\'94\
\'93What is it with the Elvi, they have a holy momma 
\f2\i and
\f1\i0  a great teacher?\'94\
\'93Interesting that you should observe that, your Supreme Corporateness.\'94 Gerry flicked through a series of slides.\
\'93These are from the recent Shakti wedding.\'94 The screen showed pictures of Chantara and the High Elvis sitting together, and of him throwing punches in the fight that broke out.\
\'93I was there!\'94 Dunhilton said in shock.\
Gerry nodded. \'93This is from Alexander Shakti\'92s broadcast after the Scarlett Shower Surgeon had been killed.\'94 The short clip showed Shakti presenting to camera with Haloren Smythe\'92s body on the floor and a man kneeling over him. Gerry froze the vid at a point that would most clearly show the kneelers face.\
\'93Chantara!\'94 Dunhilton almost spat. \'93I knew he was involved in those killings somehow.\'94\
\'93And now to Elvi concert in The Domain.\'94\
\'93I expect you to get to the bottom of how they obtained approval for that,\'94 Dunhilton said.\
The screen showed an image of Chantara surrounded by doting girls. The High Elvis sat on an esky nearby. Chantara and the High Elvis were clearly engaged in conversation. The next image showed an image, from square on in front, of the VIP platform. Two thrones were occupied by Sarah Jacobson and an Elis.\
\'93The second throne is Chantara\'92s, but intel says he did to occupy it all day,\'94 Gerry said.\
\'93Wait! Is that \'85 Eloise Shakti \'85 in an office chair?\'94 Dunhilton could hardly believe what he was seeing.\
\'93We now have solid intel that Sarah Jacobson aka the Holy Momma, Dr Katherine Logan, aka Holy Aunt Kathy\'85\'94 Gerry pointed to her on the screen. \'93\'85 and \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 Detective Superintendent Hayley Lanning, aka Holy Aunt Hayley\'85\'94 Gerry pointed at Hayley. \'93\'85 are residing at Eloise Shakti\'92s Sublime Point compound in the mountains.\'94\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
Gerry flicked to another image of the VIP platform, from far enough back to include engineering floor of the tower behind. Standing at the railing was a man who looked down on the platform as if he controlled everything.\
\'93Chantara again,\'94 Dunhilton said flatly. He was over being surprised.\
The next image was of Chantara on stage at the protest on Bent Street plaza, apparently leading his gullible flock.\
Gerry flicked though a series of pictures of 
\fs20 SHAKTI ENTERPRISES 
\fs22 landing or taking off from what looked like a park in a run-down part of town.\
Dunhilton was incredulous. \'93Are they landing on the ground?\'94\
\'93Since the day after the Bent Street Plaza incident until yesterday they\'92ve made two flights a day into the Ghetto.\'94 Gerry flicked to a vid that he hadn\'92t press play on yet.\
\'93I\'92ve seen this one,\'94 Dunhilton said. \'93It\'92s the inauguration of the High Elvis.\'94\
\'93It\'92s the inauguration of the 
\f2\i second
\f1\i0  High Elvis. The first one expired at Bent Street Plaza. The figure standing in the spa bath, dressed like an Elvis impersonator, is Chantara. I\'92ll let him speak for himself here. Listen carefully to what he has to say, your Supreme Corporateness.\'94 Gerry pressed play.\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f2\i \cf2 \'93The cure has been spreading for a while now, maybe months. Let\'92s not get bogged down on who infected who or when or in whose bathroom or grandparents\'92 pantry. If you\'92re here in this room right now, feeling better than you\'92ve ever felt before, then you probably already carry the cure. And there\'92s a fast way to spread it, and it is joyous news, my beloved Elvi. I give you the First Decree of the Great Teacher and the Holy Aunts.\
\'93Go forth and hump!\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\fi360\sl220\qj\partightenfactor0

\f1\i0 \cf2 Dunhilton drew his conclusion more than twenty seconds before he could bring himself to utter it. \'93Eloise Shakti already has a cure to the Lentil Virus.\'94
